>> E.g. take {brife} meaning "wind". A computer algorithm created it by mix=
ing Chinese "fen" and English "breeze".
>>=20
>> What is more {brife} can mean both "wind" and "breeze". In other words y=
ou get words that neither sound like words in the source languages, nor hav=
e the same meaning as in the source languages.
>>=20
